---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Signature from '~/components/Signature.astro';
import { site } from '~/config';
import { withBase } from '~/lib/url';

// Photos on this page are imported by name, one line each. They live in the
// same folder as every other photo on the site, so a photo used here can be in
// the gallery and in an update as well, stored once.
import grad from '~/content/photos/2026-04-29-grad.jpg';
import indo from '~/content/photos/2026-06-05-indo.jpg'

const portraitFiles = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>(
  '../assets/portrait.{jpg,jpeg,png,webp,avif}',
  { eager: true },
);
const portrait = Object.values(portraitFiles)[0]?.default;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description={`About ${site.name}.`}
  image={portrait?.src}
>
  <article class="article">
    <header class="article__header">
      <h1>About me</h1>
      <p class="article__summary">
        My story, my vision, and what's next!
      </p>
    </header>

    {/* The photo sits beside the opening lines rather than on its own between
        the heading and the story — the same idea as the note on the home page,
        so there is a face to go with the first words you read. Write the story
        itself below, starting at "How I got here". */}
    <div class:list={['about__intro', !portrait && 'about__intro--no-portrait']}>
      {
        portrait && (
          <Image
            class="about__portrait"
            src={portrait}
            alt={site.portraitAlt}
            width={288}
            densities={[1, 2]}
            loading="eager"
          />
        )
      }

      <div>
        <p>
          Thank you for visiting this site! I’m Ethan, and I’m currently training to be full-time campus staff with SOON Movement Global. This is a place where I can share what God is doing through this season with the people who pray for and support me.
        </p>
        <p>
          I hope this site can be an encouragement to you, while also serving as a memorial stone of God’s faithfulness and grace in my life.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How I got here</h2>
      {/* A photo written like this matches the ones in an update: a <figure>
          with the caption under it. "figure--text-width" keeps it to the width
          of the words either side of it; drop that class and it spreads wider
          than the text, the way the photos in an update do.

          `sizes` mirrors the CSS that lays it out — the text column, 680px at
          its widest — so the browser does not download a photo far larger than
          it shows. Change one and change the other. */}
      <figure class="figure--text-width">
        <Image
          src={grad}
          alt="The Northeastern SOONjangs at Krentzman Quad."
          width={1360}
          widths={[480, 680, 1020, 1360, 1700]}
          sizes="(max-width: 720px) calc(100vw - 2.5rem), 680px"
        />
        <figcaption>
          The 2025–26 Northeastern SOONjangs.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        SOON Movement has been an incredible blessing in my life. After a difficult first year of college, God met me through SOON in my second year and showed me that His love and a life with Him were greater than anything I could chase on my own.
      </p>
      <p>
        After recommitting my life to Christ, I was given many opportunities throughout college to serve Him, pursue Him, and love others. As graduation approached and I began considering what came next, God revealed a deep desire in my heart to continue reaching college students in His name, investing in His kingdom, and empowering them to go and fulfill the Great Commission.
      </p>
      <p>
        After a season of wrestling with this calling and surrounding myself with people who faithfully supported me in prayer, I ultimately decided to take a step of faith and pursue full-time ministry with SOON.
      </p>

      <h2>My vision</h2>
      <figure class="figure--text-width">
        <Image
          src={indo}
          alt="Two students next to a train in Indonesia"
          width={1360}
          widths={[480, 680, 1020, 1360, 1700]}
          sizes="(max-width: 720px) calc(100vw - 2.5rem), 680px"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Summer Missions is one way students are sent to share the Gospel.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        God has given me a story of redemption that I believe He can use to reach students who are searching for something greater than what the world offers.
      </p>
      <p>
        I believe that the college students of today will be the future leaders of the world. My desire is to reach students in His name, invest in them throughout this formative and often difficult season, lead them to Christ, and send them out to change the world.
      </p>
      <p>
        I want to see students transformed by the Gospel and sent out to bring hope to the people and places God places before them.
      </p>

      <h2>Staying in touch</h2>
      <p>
        I hope to post regular updates on the <a href={withBase('/updates')}>updates page</a>, so feel free to bookmark it and check back from time to time!
      </p>
      <p>
        Each update will include ways you can pray for me and what God is doing in this season. Your prayers are one of the greatest ways you can support me, and I’m incredibly grateful for them.
      </p>

      {
        site.contact.email && (
          <p>
            If you have any prayer requests, questions, or just want to reach out, please contact me at <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
          </p>
        )
      }

      <Signature />
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
